Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Infra Bundles", "Title",
 CellID->509267359,ExpressionUUID->"4ddb5767-1f00-4973-a411-49eacd07850d"],

Cell["\<\
We start with a finite graph and a projection of its vertices. Equal fibers, \
lift existence, unique lifting and bundle structure are separate properties. \
Sections and complete connections add choices to this data.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f82de1a2-0176-4efa-af21-24165d4d1cc0"],

Cell["Topological language and finite readings", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"f487ec0e-bb2d-4f1a-9efd-84450224efcc"],

Cell["\<\
The finite object is a graph with a vertex projection. The following \
dictionary distinguishes its exact conditions from the additional structures \
of continuous topology.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a00d246b-0470-4eaf-a10b-d09726576579"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "2bd387ef-fd6c-4f7d-9b0a-14effc5e9d85"], Cell[
    "Topological notion", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"f241df29-db27-40f5-8011-51fbfe4f64a8"],
     Cell["Finite infra reading", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"df1cff62-7f5e-47a7-ab59-b61cfe90e7ca"],
     Cell["Qualification", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"7ff821aa-4823-44ab-933b-212aa8099998"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "075e3127-bad2-4763-9870-673fd3a59fbd"], Cell[
    "Projection from total space to base", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "21cd4b83-f9fd-4e96-a045-cb4d77703e5d"], Cell["\<\
InfraFiberedGraph with InfraTotalSpace, InfraBaseSpace and InfraProjection\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"1991f3d0-8ae1-4fdf-ad7d-a3b6c99cd15e"], 
    Cell["\<\
The base graph is reconstructed from projected edges; no topology is part of \
the inert object.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"f3f56eb9-438f-49b6-bf1f-42de04bbd20f"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "b6da0fba-59a5-4df6-801a-853b7fa820fb"], Cell[
    "Serre or Hurewicz fibration", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "effc75c7-e186-4b69-ad68-4c66163b1edf"], Cell["\<\
InfraFibrationQ asks for a lift of every base edge from every starting vertex\
\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"dbbcf73b-e552-4e3e-8f0a-8f433ac4fd8b"], 
    Cell["\<\
This is weak edge-lift existence, not a homotopy-lifting axiom.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"17ee36c9-f805-4e88-920b-c83785de85e1"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "acdee622-b539-4bdc-9eed-d3534e85c772"], Cell[
    "Covering space", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "92a5f31e-ae59-4480-9ff3-8e000ede4ce9"], Cell["\<\
InfraCoveringQ gives edgeless fibers and a bijection on vertex neighbourhoods\
\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"acbdef76-d953-4304-bf38-80345c8083e1"], 
    Cell["\<\
The graph-covering condition has the usual covering interpretation under \
graph realization. Sheet counts can differ across base components.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"3469fbe8-70e4-4521-bd79-dacb04d42636"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "78dabbdf-9ed1-4deb-bd7f-4d7dcbea841b"], Cell[
    "Fiber bundle", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "70a5f841-56c6-4118-8545-d63ab9ed5196"], Cell["\<\
InfraFiberBundleQ gives a common fiber graph and adjacency-preserving \
transverse matchings\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"f12faad0-7879-4b90-8387-8bfe515c0e1a"], 
    Cell["\<\
This is an edgewise Cartesian graph bundle. Realizing its edges alone does \
not supply topological product charts or filled squares.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"bcd67e07-faae-425b-8052-c4a1214163d2"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "94a180e2-8c4d-4a23-a50c-96c29650683e"], Cell[
    "Section", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "41476b0f-9c63-4a7c-910e-0a826de0483a"], Cell[
    "InfraSection chooses a right inverse on a base domain", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"7e5f4cbf-80e4-46fc-a4a6-280dbc6fbadd"], Cell["\<\
InfraContinuousSectionQ asks for adjacency preservation on that domain.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"7aaa7b9a-5363-4a14-95fd-f3fdce101b2c"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "bd3e48af-9f17-49ff-bc13-8c54a08dd58a"], Cell[
    "Connection and parallel transport", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "3eb68766-01dc-4c19-856f-381cb7700cc3"], Cell["\<\
InfraConnection selects complete fiber matchings; transport composes them\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"0d332584-bbff-4df6-978d-e82c03ef1f25"], 
    Cell["\<\
This is finite bijective transport. Preserving a fiber graph is an additional \
condition.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"d6d493c2-be99-4cb3-b5ab-4a8e727561d1"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "49129c16-0938-4a2f-9035-0368a299f110"], Cell[
    "Infra-only transverse local conditions", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "ba314229-27df-4a5d-9dc5-44521a128bfd"], Cell["\<\
InfraAtMostOneEdgeLiftQ and InfraFibrationQ read injectivity and surjectivity \
on transverse neighbours\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"2fffd6bb-61da-4b0d-9825-d749c3ae9470"], 
    Cell["\<\
Vertical neighbours are excluded; the conditions do not assert local \
injectivity or surjectivity in a chosen topology.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"d1689791-d5cc-4da6-bbf0-031aeb45c8c0"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "d9da5286-879b-4fec-a74f-3b37d73c7789"], Cell[
    "Infra-only multiplicity and equitable partition", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"0e11b4e9-31b6-40d6-9442-4ec6054e947b"], Cell["\<\
InfraEdgeLiftMultiplicity counts transverse neighbours, including zeros\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"1508387b-c26d-41b0-a2c0-d39c6201550b"], 
    Cell["\<\
Constancy within each fiber is transverse equitability; full equitability \
also needs constant vertical degree.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"e5368329-0a4b-4c52-8330-1791bac8ad38"]}
  }]], "3ColumnTableMod",ExpressionUUID->"cbc69cf2-75b2-4f6a-9fe0-\
07c6f1a760f9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For the continuous definitions, see ",
 ButtonBox["Hatcher, Algebraic Topology, Sections 1.3 and 4.2",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://pi.math.cornell.edu/~hatcher/AT/AT.pdf"], None}],
 ". The finite definitions and their implications are developed below."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a900e94c-f633-472e-99b6-636f280fbb65"],

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ce182108-0687-4800-841b-44db01b86a10"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", " ", "\"\<WolframInstitute`InfraGeometry`\>\"", " ", 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"ffda5b5a-becc-44cf-8e90-8f8cd74bed45"],

Cell["Total space, projection and fibers", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"876399cb-7f1c-414a-9422-8eae2912cb6a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A ",
 StyleBox["fibered graph", "TI"],
 " consists of a finite simple undirected unweighted untagged graph ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["E", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4757d93d-fab5-402b-8eb7-cb005c95173b"],
 " and a map ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Pi]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fd21f07f-e2af-4ecc-bfe2-9dd33fbfc1f3"],
 " on its vertices. The ",
 StyleBox["base graph", "TI"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["B", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b3aae89e-7c82-4c28-9e86-a9965642b691"],
 " has vertex set ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Pi]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f3dbc050-6949-4550-bddb-6af5fd9a8038"],
 ". Distinct base vertices are adjacent exactly when some total edge joins \
their preimages. The ",
 StyleBox["fiber", "TI"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["p", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e5abaf73-9182-4c5d-b2ee-da74337c7f57"],
 " is the induced graph on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f470b3c1-5bf0-44c9-b03a-52df2abd5a86"],
 ". A total edge is ",
 StyleBox["vertical", "TI"],
 " when both endpoints project to the same vertex, and ",
 StyleBox["transverse", "TI"],
 " otherwise."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6f1375f7-a647-4d3e-b050-007e68ecd773"],

Cell["\<\
The object carries no drawing, connection or lifting axiom. The base includes \
isolated projection values, and projection collapses vertical edges. The \
empty graph with empty projection is allowed.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"17fc8e8a-83ba-4a2e-ab4f-5642ba0d60ab"],

